# Iconify: string literals only

`react-native-iconify` transforms icons at build time. The `icon` prop **must** be a string literal in JSX.

## Do

```tsx
<Iconify icon="heroicons:magnifying-glass" size={20} color={color} />

// Shared wrappers: accept ReactNode / render props, not icon name strings
icon={<Iconify icon="heroicons:exclamation-triangle" size={32} color={color} />}
renderIcon={(color) => <Iconify icon="heroicons:arrow-path" size={18} color={color} />}
```

## Do not

```tsx
const name = "heroicons:x-mark";
<Iconify icon={name} />           // fails: dynamic
<Iconify icon={props.icon} />     // fails: prop variable
<Iconify icon={condition ? "a" : "b"} /> // avoid; use separate branches with literals
```

When building reusable components that need icons, take `React.ReactNode` or `(color: string) => React.ReactNode` — never a dynamic icon name string passed into `Iconify`.
